<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="crafted-gear">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_mace_39.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Crafted &amp; Profession Gear for Balance Druids</span></h2>Crafted items are, for the most part, no longer restricted by profession, meaning that even if you aren't a Leatherworker, you can equip anything Leatherworkers craft. There are a few notable exceptions to this: the Engineer goggles and the Alchemist trinket. There is also the Inscription staff, which is bound to account.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a> is a very strong trinket made with Inscription. It will remain one of our best trinkets until we can get our hands on 2 Heroic raid trinkets. It will be <b>extremely expensive</b>. Players without a massive budget are advised to look at other uses for their gold.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85829/nightfire-robe">
<img alt="Nightfire Robe" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_robe_leather_raiddruid_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Nightfire Robe</span></a> is an item made by Leatherworkers. As it is an item with Mastery that competes for the same spot as tier pieces, it is not recommended to go for this one once we have access to tier pieces.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=85827/liferuned-leather-gloves">
<img alt="Liferuned Leather Gloves" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_glove_leather_raidmonk_l_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Liferuned Leather Gloves</span></a> is an item made by Leatherworkers. It has a good distribution of secondary stats, but it does compete against tier pieces, which makes it hard to slot into our gear set.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=77535/camouflage-retinal-armor">
<img alt="Camouflage Retinal Armor" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_helmet_goggles_pandariatradeskill_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Camouflage Retinal Armor</span></a> is exclusive to Engineers. You can choose your two preferred secondary stats for this item, making it always be a strong pick.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> is exclusive to Alchemists. It is very strong even though it has a low item level. It will last until you have access to Normal raid trinkets or a Relic of Yu'lon.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79340/inscribed-crane-staff">
<img alt="Inscribed Crane Staff" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_staff_2h_pandariatradeskill_c_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Inscribed Crane Staff</span></a> is made with Inscription and is bound to account. This means you can craft it on an alt and send it to your main, although you can not buy it from other players. This also gives you the opportunity to send it between multiple characters with just one craft.</div></li></ul>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="trinkets">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/creatureportrait_twilightshammer_dragonegg_01.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Pre-Raid Balance Druid Trinkets</span></h2>DPS Trinkets are straightforward. Generally speaking, pick the highest listed item for the best effect.<h5 class="heading-size-5" id="best-trinkets">Best Trinkets</h5>Balance Druids will want to use two passive trinkets. The active trinkets are only something we would use if we lack a second passive trinket.<br/>
<br/>
<ins>Passive Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=79331/relic-of-yulon">
<img alt="Relic of Yu'lon" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_inscription_trinket_dragon.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Yu'lon</span></a> is a very powerful trinket. With a lot of Intellect and a strong Intellect proc that has high uptime, this trinket is far stronger than its item level would suggest.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86907/essence-of-terror">
<img alt="Essence of Terror" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pvp_trinket.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Essence of Terror</span></a> provides a lot of Intellect as well as a powerful Haste proc. This trinket has much lower uptime than the other trinkets it competes against. To compensate, however, the effect is powerful, making it especially powerful during our opener.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=75274/zen-alchemist-stone">
<img alt="Zen Alchemist Stone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pet_scorchedstone.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Zen Alchemist Stone</span></a> has a very strong proc, allowing it to compete as one of our best pre-raid trinkets.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=86792/light-of-the-cosmos">
<img alt="Light of the Cosmos" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_offhand_ulduarraid_d_03.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Light of the Cosmos</span></a> has a decent chunk of Haste as well as a high uptime on the Intellect buff, making it a very desirable trinket overall.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81192/vision-of-the-predator">
<img alt="Vision of the Predator" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_20.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Vision of the Predator</span></a> is the weakest passive trinket we have. It is, however, stronger than our choices for active trinkets.</div></li></ul>
<ins>Active Trinkets</ins>
<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=89081/blossom-of-pure-snow">
<img alt="Blossom of Pure Snow" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/item_herbd.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Blossom of Pure Snow</span></a> is a decent trinket. Its on-use should be used right before we apply our DoTs, and then we reapply the DoTs again just before it expires, so that we get maximum value out of the effect.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=81263/flashfrozen-resin-globule">
<img alt="Flashfrozen Resin Globule" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_21.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Flashfrozen Resin Globule</span></a> is helpful during early gearing while still working towards Hit cap. It's not a strong trinket overall and should be the first one you aim to replace.</div></li></ul>
<div data-inserted-ad-group="2" style="display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; justify-content: center; align-items: center;">
<div data-ad="inline-leaderboard" data-multiformat="true" id="ad_inline-leaderboard_2" style="width: 728px; height: 250px; background: rgba(136, 136, 136, 0.133); --ad-width: 728px; --ad-height: 250px;">
<div data-house-ad="true" data-house-show-before-ad-request="" style="width: 728px; height: 90px;">
<a href="https://tidd.ly/4cE3lxF" target="_blank">
<img alt="ad" src="//r2.rev.iq/wowhead.com/House_BlizzGear_Collectables_728x90.webp"/></a></div></div></div>
<h2 class="heading-size-2 heading-bar" id="hit-expertise">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/ability_marksmanship.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Reaching Hit and Expertise Cap for Balance Druids</span></h2>In Mists of Pandaria our Hit cap is 15%. Spirit still converts to Hit for us, and now Expertise also contributes to our Hit cap. At 15% Hit, our spells will no longer miss raid bosses. This requires a total combined Spirit, Hit and Expertise of 5100. Normally we will have no Expertise, although we sometimes have a small amount of it from gems. Reaching Hit cap is very important for us, both because of it being an efficient way to get DPS and because it makes the rotation more predictable.<h3 class="heading-size-3 heading-bar" id="gemming">
<span data-markup-content-target="1">
<span class="iconmedium" data-color="c11" data-contiguous="true" data-env="mists" data-game="wow" data-kind="round" data-tree="mists">
<ins class="lazy-load-background" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/medium/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_uncut_purple.jpg");'></ins>
<del></del></span> Best Gems for Balance Druids</span></h3>Gems are a great place to grab any Hit that we may be missing. This can be especially useful when aiming for Socket Bonuses, as <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76651/energized-wild-jade">
<img alt="Energized Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Energized Wild Jade</span></a> and <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76686/purified-imperial-amethyst">
<img alt="Purified Imperial Amethyst" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_purple.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Purified Imperial Amethyst</span></a> are the only good ways to utilize a Blue Socket if we want the bonus.<br/>
<br/>You will generally aim to fill all Blue Sockets then use reforging to ensure Hit cap. If you're still under Hit cap afterwards, then using <a class="q3 icontiny" data-contiguous="true" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/mop-classic/item=76651/energized-wild-jade">
<img alt="Energized Wild Jade" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_gem_x4_rare_cut_green.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Energized Wild Jade</span></a> in Yellow Sockets is also an option.<br/>
<br/>Once you're at 5100 Hit Rating, things become complex. The general rule of thumb is to prioritize Intellect while grabbing Haste in Yellow Sockets if you are below 5273 Haste rating, without Tier 14 4-piece bonus. If you have Tier 14 4-piece bonus <i>or</i> above 5273 Haste rating, you will instead aim to grab Critical Strike rating from Yellow Sockets.<br/>
<br/>There will also be situations where using pure Haste or Critical Strike gems is better than Intellect gems. This can not be determined without a sim, and so for the best results, it is recommended to always sim yourself.<ul class="exclude-units">
<li>
